## 3. Consent Management Framework

### 3.1 Adaptive, Neurodivergent-Friendly Consent Table

| Element            | Standard Approach                         | Neurodivergent-First Upgrade                |
|--------------------|-------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|
| Language           | Legal/technical wording                   | Plain, option for visual, audio, examples   |
| Accessibility      | One-size-fits-all forms                   | Toggleable complexity/length, assistive options |
| Timing             | Point-in-time agreement                   | Regular, scheduled reminders and opt-outs   |
| Role Clarity       | User vs. system responsibilities unclear  | Dashboard with who, what, why, when, where  |
| Feedback           | Passive withdrawal only                   | “Amend, pause, delete” + proactive alerts   |

#### 3.2 Features

- **Granular Control**: Select specific data sharing (modality, topic, time-window, squad).
- **Logging & Audit**: All consent actions timestamped, with quick history review.
- **Guardrails**: System prevents data usage outside consent scope or upon withdrawal.
- **Contextual Education**: Micro-explanations (tooltips, videos) clarify risks and potential benefits for each data type.
- **Community Accountability**: Consent and privacy logs are peer-reviewed by a neurodivergent oversight board where feasible.

Integrate regular “consent check-ins,” especially at points when new features are added, policies change, or data is being shared externally or with new modules. Notification preferences themselves must be adjustable to avoid overwhelm or cognitive overload.

