## 5. Verification & Fact-Checking Module

### 5.1 Multi-Tiered Verification Framework

Both lived experience and clinical data demand robust verification to filter inaccuracies, intentional misinformation, or hallucinations, without suppressing marginalized or minority perspectives.

#### 5.2 Verification Techniques Table

| Data Type        | Primary Verification | Supplementary Approaches                         |
|------------------|---------------------|--------------------------------------------------|
| Lived Experience | Peer review, narrative triangulation | Source-tracking, digital provenance, semantic similarity clustering |
| Clinical Data    | Cross-reference with standards (DSM, ICD, clinical notes) | Automated fact-check against EHRs, literature validation |
| Sourced Content  | Automated fact-checking, citation risk scoring | Bias detection, provenance graph, XAI explanations |

#### 5.3 Verification System Features

- **Peer Narrative Review**: Community members (opted-in, trained or credentialed) review stories for accuracy, harmful content, outlier flagging, or suggest contextual tags. Minority voices are not down-weighted, but flagged for further discussion/disambiguation if disputed.
- **Automated Fact-Checking**: Leverage tools such as Sourcely, AI Fact-Checking Tool, Content Bias Analyzer, and Data Chart Validator. Each module provides rapid truth-risk scoring, citation suggestions, and discrepancy detection—complemented by human review for nuanced or context-rich lived experience data.
- **Provenance & Trust Graphs**: All data points linked to source and transformation lineage (e.g., chain from self-report, through automated summary, through review, to derived model input), supporting full traceability and “point-in-graph” explanations.
- **Bias & Hallucination Audits**: Quantitative metrics for hallucinations or omissions, based on graph-matching and peer review, are regularly updated and surfaced in system dashboards.
- **User Transparency**: Users can track their own data lifecycle—what has been reviewed, flagged, verified, or used in aggregate—via an accessible dashboard.

#### 5.4 Verification Metrics Table

| Metric           | Description                                     | Benchmark / Tool                  |
|------------------|-------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------|
| Fact Support     | % of claims supported by trusted reference       | >90% (VeriFact, Foster AI)        |
| Peer Agreement   | % reviewer agreement on lived stories            | >80%                              |
| Hallucination Rate | Undetected/unverified facts per dataset        | <5% per batch                     |
| Omission Rate    | Relevant true facts missing per dataset          | <10% per batch                    |

