## 10. Regulatory Compliance and Data Privacy

### 10.1 Key Requirements Table

| Regulation/Standard          | Mandatory Actions                                 |
|------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|
| EU AI Act (2024)| Bias audits, risk categorization, human oversight, transparency |
| GDPR/CCPA                    | Data minimization, deletion, breach notification   |
| Accessibility Laws (WCAG, POUR) | Usable by assistive tech, multi-modal input/output |
| Data Trust Framework (UK, EY) | Data trust score, governance, consent logs         |

- **High-Risk Models**: All AI influencing diagnosis, education, or employment must be flagged as “high-risk”; subject to continuous bias auditing and explainability standards.
- **Right to Contest**: Users must be able to review, dispute, or appeal algorithmic outcomes, with recourse to human review within reasonable time.
- **Open Data Option**: Where applicable, empower open data contributions, but always with consent and the ability to “unshare” retrospectively if needed.
- **Secure Data Lifecycles**: End-to-end encryption, transparent retention/deletion policies, incident reporting infrastructure.

